{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Even [from a day].</b> The meaning: I am El before there was [a name for] day; therefore the word \"even.\"" "<b>[From a day].</b> From the being of day." "<b>I am He.</b> And since I am El, who can escape My hand?" "<b>I act.</b> My desire and my will; and who can reverse My deed?"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:44.467969549Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}